      "problem": "BLOCKING wrong canonical fact at fastapi_backend.trusted_host_validation@python_fastapi_backend_developer: f3/tb3/tb5 say www_redirect redirects an 'allowed non-www host' to its www form. Starlette's implementation (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Kludex/starlette/main/starlette/middleware/trustedhost.py, __call__) instead immediately passes an already allowed host to the app. A redirect occurs only for an otherwise invalid host when the exact 'www.' + host entry is present in allowed_hosts and www_redirect is true. For example, allowed_hosts=['example.com'] accepts example.com without redirect; allowed_hosts=['www.example.com'] can redirect example.com. Therefore f1's unconditional claim that every nonmatching host returns 400 also omits this redirect exception.",
